"text": "So why is AI so confidently wrong? Because sounding right comes from patterns in language, and being right takes evidence the model doesn't always have.\n\nSo when an answer matters, don't ask whether it sounds right. Ask what the evidence is, and whether it actually says this.\n\nWorks on chatbots. Works pretty well on people, too.\n\nThis is Future Got Weird. AI moves fast; we make it make sense. New episodes twice a week, if you'd like to subscribe.",
